23
00:00:59,155 --> 00:01:00,877
This installation is closed.

24
00:01:03,213 --> 00:01:04,575
Here's the part that's real.

25
00:01:05,156 --> 00:01:07,858
In 2011, officers training at U.S.

26
00:01:07,878 --> 00:01:09,939
Strategic Command wrote a plan for a

27
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,662
zombie apocalypse. CONPLAN 8888.

28
00:01:14,302 --> 00:01:16,444
It was a classroom exercise, chosen

29
00:01:16,504 --> 00:01:18,447
because no one could ever mistake it for a

30
00:01:18,546 --> 00:01:22,150
real threat. But the paper is real, and so

31
00:01:22,290 --> 00:01:25,632
are its orders. One table says, lockdown

32
00:01:25,733 --> 00:01:28,174
for 30 days. The written orders go

33
00:01:28,254 --> 00:01:30,772
further. Shelter all mission essential

34
00:01:30,811 --> 00:01:33,412
personnel in place for at least 40 days.

35
00:01:34,132 --> 00:01:35,634
Jo is mission essential.

36
00:01:36,054 --> 00:01:39,055
You are not. The real plan says nothing

37
00:01:39,114 --> 00:01:40,516
about people waiting at a gate.

38
00:01:41,075 --> 00:01:43,996
That part is our story, and in our story,

39
00:01:44,337 --> 00:01:46,298
this gate is not going to open.

40
00:01:48,058 --> 00:01:49,099
Listen to the horns.

41
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:51,439
Everyone is a dinner bell.

42
00:01:52,099 --> 00:01:54,001
The plan's authors guessed how the dead

43
00:01:54,040 --> 00:01:56,341
would move. They wrote that zombies cannot

44
00:01:56,421 --> 00:01:59,097
drive, climb, or swim and that they would

45
00:01:59,177 --> 00:02:01,599
follow the roads. Behind you is the

46
00:02:01,679 --> 00:02:03,718
interstate. Stay with the crowd and the

47
00:02:03,759 --> 00:02:05,599
light, or walk into the dark.

48
00:02:06,299 --> 00:02:09,441
You walk. A mile east, black against the

49
00:02:09,480 --> 00:02:11,602
sky, there's an old grain elevator.

50
00:02:12,181 --> 00:02:14,741
Its steel ladder starts 12 feet up so kids

51
00:02:14,801 --> 00:02:17,163
can't climb it. From the top, you'd see

52
00:02:17,203 --> 00:02:20,003
the whole base. Halfway across the field,

53
00:02:20,183 --> 00:02:22,884
you hear a boy, maybe 10, in a red hoodie,

54
00:02:23,284 --> 00:02:25,824
standing between the cars saying one word

55
00:02:26,125 --> 00:02:27,026
over and over.

56
00:02:28,804 --> 00:02:31,286
His name is Eli. His father walked to the

57
00:02:31,325 --> 00:02:32,806
gate an hour ago to argue.

58
00:02:33,206 --> 00:02:34,127
He hasn't come back.

59
00:02:34,848 --> 00:02:37,150
You don't decide. Your hand just takes

60
00:02:37,210 --> 00:02:40,192
his. Behind you, the horns begin to stop.

61
00:02:40,671 --> 00:02:43,153
One by one. At the foot of the elevator,

62
00:02:43,294 --> 00:02:44,955
your flashlight finds an aluminum

63
00:02:44,995 --> 00:02:46,816
extension ladder lying in the weeds.

64
00:02:47,256 --> 00:02:49,677
You raise it. It just reaches the first

65
00:02:49,717 --> 00:02:52,038
steel rung. Eli climbs first.

66
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:54,741
Then, from the narrow landing, you haul

67
00:02:54,781 --> 00:02:56,682
the ladder up after you and lay it along

68
00:02:56,703 --> 00:02:59,211
the rail. Now there is nothing below you

69
00:02:59,270 --> 00:03:01,311
but 12 feet of smooth concrete.

70
00:03:01,812 --> 00:03:03,731
If the planners guessed right, nothing

71
00:03:03,812 --> 00:03:05,032
dead can follow you up.

72
00:03:06,812 --> 00:03:09,054
Dawn, you count what you have.

73
00:03:09,854 --> 00:03:10,794
One bottle of water.

74
00:03:11,455 --> 00:03:13,575
A granola bar Eli is pretending not to

75
00:03:13,635 --> 00:03:15,317
watch. A pocket knife.

76
00:03:15,917 --> 00:03:18,437
A phone with no signal and 31%.

77
00:03:19,057 --> 00:03:21,079
From up here, the base looks peaceful.

78
00:03:21,639 --> 00:03:23,479
Somewhere in there, Jo is safe.

79
00:03:24,159 --> 00:03:26,241
Down in the field, hundreds have gathered

80
00:03:26,281 --> 00:03:28,979
along the fence. Emergency guidance says a

81
00:03:29,139 --> 00:03:31,700
gallon of water per person per day, at

82
00:03:31,741 --> 00:03:33,201
least half of it just to drink.

83
00:03:33,763 --> 00:03:34,603
There are two of you.

84
00:03:34,984 --> 00:03:36,003
You have one bottle.

85
00:03:36,585 --> 00:03:38,145
The planners wrote that rain will be

86
00:03:38,246 --> 00:03:40,307
vitally important and that streams and

87
00:03:40,367 --> 00:03:41,769
rivers will be unreliable.

88
00:03:42,508 --> 00:03:44,169
On day three, it rains.

89
00:03:44,770 --> 00:03:46,752
You stretch your jacket across the walkway

90
00:03:46,832 --> 00:03:48,873
and funnel every drop into the bottle,

91
00:03:49,234 --> 00:03:51,536
into the wrapper, into your cupped hands.

92
00:03:52,236 --> 00:03:54,098
Eli laughs for the first time.

93
00:03:54,657 --> 00:03:55,679
Remember that laugh.

94
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:56,920
You'll need it.

95
00:03:58,530 --> 00:04:00,591
One storm won't last forty days.

96
00:04:01,312 --> 00:04:03,453
You need something to catch rain and store

97
00:04:03,513 --> 00:04:05,894
it. There's a farmhouse half a mile north.

98
00:04:06,534 --> 00:04:08,156
The plan made one more guess.

99
00:04:08,716 --> 00:04:10,836
The infected kind might be less active

100
00:04:10,877 --> 00:04:11,818
when the sun is bright.

101
00:04:12,397 --> 00:04:14,718
A guess. Written in a classroom.

102
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:18,401
At noon, under a hard white sun, you lower

103
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:19,802
the ladder and climb down.

104
00:04:20,523 --> 00:04:22,543
One rule. If you're not back when the

105
00:04:22,584 --> 00:04:25,084
tower's shadow touches the fence, Eli

106
00:04:25,125 --> 00:04:26,565
pushes the ladder into the wheat.

107
00:04:27,045 --> 00:04:28,067
Then nobody comes up.

108
00:04:28,487 --> 00:04:30,869
not even you. The farmhouse gives you a

109
00:04:30,908 --> 00:04:34,230
blue tarp, two 5-gallon buckets, food, a

110
00:04:34,290 --> 00:04:36,651
first aid kit, a hand crank emergency

111
00:04:36,730 --> 00:04:39,492
radio, and the thing that matters most, a

112
00:04:39,572 --> 00:04:41,774
jug of plain, unscented bleach.

113
00:04:42,413 --> 00:04:44,634
On the way back, one of them is standing

114
00:04:44,675 --> 00:04:45,694
in the tower's shade.

115
00:04:46,276 --> 00:04:48,475
Just standing, facing the base.

116
00:04:49,216 --> 00:04:51,218
You lie in the wheat until a cloud covers

117
00:04:51,278 --> 00:04:52,697
the sun and it drifts away.

118
00:04:53,257 --> 00:04:55,619
At the top, Eli has both hands on the

119
00:04:55,658 --> 00:04:56,819
ladder ready to push.

120
00:04:57,401 --> 00:04:58,442
He'd started counting.

121
00:04:59,043 --> 00:05:01,244
That night, the tarp becomes a funnel over

122
00:05:01,283 --> 00:05:03,305
a bucket, and you teach him the rule that

123
00:05:03,345 --> 00:05:06,047
keeps you alive. Eight drops of bleach per

124
00:05:06,086 --> 00:05:07,228
gallon of clear water.

125
00:05:07,747 --> 00:05:10,428
Stir. Wait 30 minutes, then drink.

126
00:05:12,211 --> 00:05:14,312
On the twelfth night, headlights.

127
00:05:15,052 --> 00:05:16,913
A pickup stops at the foot of the tower.

128
00:05:17,514 --> 00:05:19,355
Three men who saw what you saw.

129
00:05:19,754 --> 00:05:21,596
The one high place for miles.

130
00:05:22,161 --> 00:05:23,341
The ladder is still down.

131
00:05:23,721 --> 00:05:26,682
You forgot. You haul it up rung over rung

132
00:05:26,781 --> 00:05:28,963
as a flashlight finds it, and fingers

133
00:05:29,062 --> 00:05:30,242
close on empty air.

134
00:05:30,762 --> 00:05:32,084
They shout for an hour.

135
00:05:32,624 --> 00:05:34,483
Then the noise brings the dead out of the

136
00:05:34,524 --> 00:05:36,745
dark, and the truck is gone, and you are

137
00:05:36,824 --> 00:05:39,644
both still breathing, very quietly, in the

138
00:05:39,685 --> 00:05:42,245
black. The dead were never the only thing

139
00:05:42,346 --> 00:05:44,807
outside the fence. Every night at nine,

140
00:05:45,067 --> 00:05:46,766
you flash your phone toward the base.

141
00:05:47,286 --> 00:05:49,807
Three short, three long, three short.

142
00:05:50,499 --> 00:05:53,081
On night 18, a window in the medical wing

143
00:05:53,141 --> 00:05:56,244
flashes back, three times, and every night

144
00:05:56,384 --> 00:05:59,026
after that. You tell Eli it's your sister,

145
00:05:59,547 --> 00:06:01,449
you don't know that, but it's the best

146
00:06:01,509 --> 00:06:02,309
thing you have.

147
00:06:04,011 --> 00:06:07,274
Then the rain stops, six dry days.

148
00:06:07,973 --> 00:06:10,415
The buckets go down an inch a day, then

149
00:06:10,497 --> 00:06:13,980
two, then nothing. The plan warns that the

150
00:06:14,060 --> 00:06:15,821
dead will be drawn to drinking water

151
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:17,603
because that's where the living have to

152
00:06:17,642 --> 00:06:20,247
go. The only water left is the creek

153
00:06:20,307 --> 00:06:21,288
behind the farmhouse.

154
00:06:21,788 --> 00:06:24,348
You go at noon. You fill both buckets with

155
00:06:24,447 --> 00:06:25,809
brown, cloudy water.

156
00:06:26,309 --> 00:06:28,528
And Eli, who promised to stay, who

157
00:06:28,588 --> 00:06:30,689
followed you anyway, slips in the mud.

158
00:06:31,110 --> 00:06:32,410
A hand comes out of the reeds.

159
00:06:32,730 --> 00:06:34,531
You pull him so hard, you both fall

160
00:06:34,571 --> 00:06:35,511
backward into the wheat.

161
00:06:35,850 --> 00:06:37,211
You run. You climb.

162
00:06:37,451 --> 00:06:39,252
You don't stop shaking until dark.

163
00:06:39,752 --> 00:06:41,872
There's a long red scratch on Eli's

164
00:06:41,932 --> 00:06:43,992
forearm. A branch, he says.

165
00:06:44,413 --> 00:06:46,745
It was a branch. That night, you let the

166
00:06:46,786 --> 00:06:48,947
water settle and pour it through a t-shirt

167
00:06:48,987 --> 00:06:51,288
before the bleach because cloudy water has

168
00:06:51,327 --> 00:06:52,348
to be filtered first.

169
00:06:52,829 --> 00:06:54,329
You do every step right.

170
00:06:54,930 --> 00:06:56,269
It doesn't make you feel safe.

171
00:06:58,071 --> 00:06:59,932
The plan has a line about this, too.

172
00:07:00,711 --> 00:07:03,153
It warns that the newly infected may deny

173
00:07:03,192 --> 00:07:04,173
what's happening to them.

174
00:07:05,173 --> 00:07:07,634
On day 27, Eli has a fever.

175
00:07:08,134 --> 00:07:10,396
Not high. He eats. He talks.

176
00:07:10,935 --> 00:07:12,716
He sleeps against your shoulder with the

177
00:07:12,757 --> 00:07:15,262
red sleeve pulled down over his arm while

178
00:07:15,302 --> 00:07:17,283
you sit awake doing the planner's math.

179
00:07:17,923 --> 00:07:19,723
They assume the infected wouldn't last

180
00:07:19,783 --> 00:07:22,045
past 40 days. That's why their whole

181
00:07:22,105 --> 00:07:23,286
strategy is to wait.

182
00:07:24,005 --> 00:07:26,187
Day 31, the rain returns.

183
00:07:26,867 --> 00:07:29,449
Day 35, the fever comes and goes.

184
00:07:29,928 --> 00:07:31,209
The scratch doesn't heal.

185
00:07:31,829 --> 00:07:34,451
And on page 30 about people who can't keep

186
00:07:34,571 --> 00:07:37,653
up, the real plan says plainly, all who

187
00:07:37,713 --> 00:07:39,774
fall behind must be left behind.

188
00:07:40,353 --> 00:07:42,194
It was written for a training exercise.

189
00:07:42,755 --> 00:07:45,076
You are not in a training exercise.

190
00:07:46,916 --> 00:07:50,276
Day 40. Before dawn, you touch Eli's

191
00:07:50,317 --> 00:07:51,838
forehead and it's burning.

192
00:07:52,497 --> 00:07:53,598
His shirt is soaked.

193
00:07:54,278 --> 00:07:56,197
When you ease the red sleeve back, the

194
00:07:56,257 --> 00:07:58,978
scratch has swollen, angry and red at the

195
00:07:59,059 --> 00:08:02,019
edges. Whatever it is, anyone at that gate

196
00:08:02,060 --> 00:08:03,220
will see it in a second.

197
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:06,240
The real plan has a detail almost no one

198
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:08,901
talks about. After at least 40 days,

199
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:11,437
patrols go out. and every report is

200
00:08:11,497 --> 00:08:13,798
broadcast in plain language on open

201
00:08:13,858 --> 00:08:15,939
channels so survivors can find them.

202
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:18,841
At dawn, the hand crank radio wakes up.

203
00:08:19,401 --> 00:08:22,043
A woman's voice. Tired, steady.

204
00:08:22,684 --> 00:08:23,644
Your sister's voice.

205
00:08:24,985 --> 00:08:26,545
To any survivors north of the

206
00:08:26,586 --> 00:08:28,408
installation, we can take two.

207
00:08:28,968 --> 00:08:30,468
Walk to the North Gate at noon.

208
00:08:30,908 --> 00:08:32,429
No injuries, no fever.

209
00:08:32,809 --> 00:08:33,609
We will check.

210
00:08:34,650 --> 00:08:35,450
A pause.

211
00:08:37,253 --> 00:08:39,274
I'm sorry. Those are the rules.

212
00:08:40,836 --> 00:08:43,519
Eli is awake. He heard every word.

213
00:08:44,239 --> 00:08:46,519
He looks down at his sleeve, then at you.

214
00:08:47,201 --> 00:08:50,101
Say I'm fine. Please say I'm fine.

215
00:08:50,623 --> 00:08:52,984
Tell the truth and they'll take you and

216
00:08:53,244 --> 00:08:56,166
only you. He stays on this tower alone

217
00:08:56,466 --> 00:08:58,647
with a fever and a ladder he can't lift.

218
00:08:59,347 --> 00:09:01,749
Lie and walk him to that gate and you're

219
00:09:01,788 --> 00:09:03,669
betting your sister's whole building on a

220
00:09:03,750 --> 00:09:05,110
scratch you can't explain.

221
00:09:05,730 --> 00:09:07,032
Your thumb is on the button.

222
00:09:07,620 --> 00:09:09,681
and below you, at the foot of the tower,

223
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:11,721
something knocks against the steel.

224
00:09:12,402 --> 00:09:13,721
Your ladder is still up here.

225
00:09:14,322 --> 00:09:15,523
Someone has brought their own.

226
00:09:16,123 --> 00:09:17,724
The plan says they can't climb.

227
00:09:18,344 --> 00:09:19,464
So who's coming up?

228
00:09:22,404 --> 00:09:23,865
This is Don't Go There.

229
00:09:24,505 --> 00:09:26,267
Tell me what you'd say into that radio,

230
00:09:26,787 --> 00:09:28,326
and tell me the day you think you'd have

231
00:09:28,346 --> 00:09:29,607
made your first mistake.

